-4e89-56c5-bc9f-13cd61512e62" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186433312}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "e5943f62-70f0-5c53-ab7a-920918d09afb" :question/math-academy-id "q-236831" :question/problem "$9-35=${{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Since $35$ is larger than $9,$ the answer will be negative.\n\nWe start by solving an easier problem:\n\n$$\n35-9\n$$\n\nNext, we carry out the subtraction:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} &  & \\,\\,\\,\\begin{aligned}\\,\\,\\,2\\end{aligned} & \\,\\,\\,\\begin{aligned}\\,\\,\\,15\\end{aligned} \\\\  &  & \\,\\,\\,3\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,5\\,\\,\\, \\\\ \\,\\,\\,\\,-\\,\\,\\,\\, &  &  & \\,\\,\\,9\\,\\,\\, \\\\  &  & \\,\\,\\,2\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,6\\,\\,\\,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n35-9=26.\n$$\n\nHowever, since our answer must be negative, we need to change the sign of the answer above. \n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n9-35=-26.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186433321 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064256 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f1c51da0-7569-50c0-b405-c74419d47ef3" :knowledge-point/title "Subtracting a Positive Number From a Non-Negative Number With Larger Numbers"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "13042cd9-3fe1-5a6e-9f68-9d984f61c24d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "312" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186433283} {:answer/id #uuid "1770c383-61fb-5018-b6c5-fdbcc32171fc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-312" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186433284} {:answer/id #uuid "1c685f83-613d-5efb-af1b-74efe04a9fc8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186433285} {:answer/id #uuid "9fe61404-3c3f-5e16-8ee3-d2435d9af2c3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-112" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186433294} {:answer/id #uuid "fc2b80ec-332b-557d-8faa-5a766f70650c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "112" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186433304}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9fe61404-3c3f-5e16-8ee3-d2435d9af2c3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-112" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186433294} :answer-field/id #uuid "fe1f0b9c-c9e8-5a12-a467-e1100119fece" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186433313}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "bceb489c-a699-54cb-aed4-c91f526fac06" :question/math-academy-id "q-6102" :question/problem "$100-212=$" :question/worked-solution "Since $212$ is larger than $100,$ the answer will be negative.\n\nWe start by solving an easier problem:\n\n$$\n212-100\n$$\n\nNext, we carry out the subtraction:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} &  & \\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\, \\\\  &  & \\,\\,\\,2\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,1\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,2\\,\\,\\, \\\\ \\,\\,\\,\\,-\\,\\,\\,\\, &  & \\,\\,\\,1\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,0\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,0\\,\\,\\, \\\\  &  & \\,\\,\\,1\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,1\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,2\\,\\,\\,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n212-100=112.\n$$\n\nHowever, since our answer must be negative, we need to change the sign of the answer above. \n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n100-212=-112\n$$"}]}
